u000fi to the particle\n                                                      multiplicity and collision geometry allows for probing the dependence of parton energy loss on the\n                                                      path-length L. We find that h\u000fi ∝ Lβ with β = 1.02−0.06\n                                                                                                            +0.09\n                                                                                                                  , consistent with the pQCD expectation of\n                                                      parton energy loss in a longitudinally expanding quark-gluon plasma. We then demonstrate that the\n                                                      azimuthal anisotropy coefficient divided by the collision eccentricity, v2 /e, follows the same scaling\n                                                      property as RAA . This scaling is observed in data, which are reproduced by the model at large\n                                                      p⊥ . Finally, a linear relationship between v2 /e and the logarithmic derivative of RAA is found and\n                                                      confirmed in data, offering an additional way to probe the L dependence of parton energy loss using\n                                                      coming measurements from LHC Run 3.\n\n\n                                            The theory of parton energy loss in quark-gluon plasma         multiplicity density n0 , h\u000fi ∝ n0 Lβ , eventually allowing\n                                         (QGP) and its associate jet quenching phenomenology               us to extract the parametric L-dependence of parton en-\n                                         in heavy ion collisions have become increasingly ma-              ergy loss in QGP. We then use this dependence to deter-\n                                         ture over the past decad